WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.935
-Our next guest is
an Academy Award-winning actress

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.238
you know from films such as
"My Cousin Vinny,"

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.672
"The Wrestler,"
and "In The Bedroom."

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:10.176
She returns as Aunt May in
"Spider-Man: No Way Home,"

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.512
which premieres exclusively
in theaters and IMAX

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.913
this Friday, December 17th.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.348
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.617
-I just feel so dumb. I didn't
realize you were miserable.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.252
-No, it was really fun.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.187
You know, that's why they call
it a fling.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.922
And we flung.
-It was fun.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.957
I could have been more fun.
I can be fun.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:27.594
-We'll hang out again.
-Wait. When do you think?

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.828
[ Rattling ]

00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:31.597
I should see what that is.
-No.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.500
No, no, no, no, no, no.
-This is what I do.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.534
-He's always coming and going.
It's not --

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.968
-Peter?
-Peter?

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.703
-Oh, no. Oh, no!
-Oh, God. Peter?

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.139
-I don't know what to do!
-Peter?

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.874
-Please welcome to the show
Marisa Tomei.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.943
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:51.317 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:58.724 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:01.160
That was a very teasing clip.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.128
-It was, on many levels.

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:04.330
-Yeah, on many levels.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.366
Now, I -- You just came back
from L.A.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.867
You were at the premiere.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.603
-It must be, I mean, always
exciting to be at a premiere,

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.939
but a premiere for a movie
this big, this anticipated,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.507
was it just a --
What was the scene like?

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:18.478
-It was the best kind of mayhem.
It was wonderful.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.781
It was like a -- more like
a rock concert than a premiere.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.850
It was so --
There was so palpably --

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.320
Everyone was so excited.
There were so many fans.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.489
Everyone was tested
and vaccinated.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.792
But it had this charge in it,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.760
like some kind of
old-fashioned, like,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.962
when I was a little girl would I
dream, like, a big premiere

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:40.566
would be like --
It's like, "The talkies are in!"

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.635
-But, yeah, the, like,
old, like, flashbulbs.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.071
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.107
-But I also heard you do not
like watching yourself on film.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.210
-No, no, I do not.
-So does that mean you don't

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.677
even sit in the audience
for a premiere?

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.513
-This one I didn't,
and I kind of regret it

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:56.849
because it was a --
it was that epic.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.719
And it will be something
I'll see in the movie theaters,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.820
because it needs to be.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.988
It's just a really,
really giant film.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.725
-So, if you were in a movie
theater and your scenes come on,

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.761
do you have to, like, do this
or can you sort of tough it out?

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.797
-Well, I don't watch like,
you know, just half of --

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.131
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.666
No, I just do this.
-Yeah, just move around? Yeah.

00:02:14.666 --> 00:02:16.268
-No.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:18.704
-Do you watch -- When you're
watching TV and old films

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.307
of yours come on, do you ever,
like, spend time with it

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.474
or do you just flip right by?

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:24.543
-I don't -- Yeah, I flip on by.

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:25.612
I haven't caught any.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.880
That hasn't ensnared me yet
really.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.048
-Oh, interesting. Alright.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.849
-Yeah.
-Okay, that's good to know.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:32.785
I want to ask about another film
you were in

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.087
because we've talked about it
a lot on this show,

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.356
"King of Staten Island,"

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.423
the Pete Davidson --
-Yes, with Pete, with Pete.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.891
-Which you were absolutely
wonderful.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.526
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:43.662
And, you know, we talked about
the fact you played his mother.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.965
I'm lucky enough to know
his mother in real life.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:50.202
And we talked about the fact,
how excited she was that you,

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.405
you know, played a fictionalized
version of her.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.140
Did you get a chance
to meet her?

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.909
-I did. I did get to meet her,
because I --

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.445
because she's so forgiving
a person.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.713
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.615
And she's incredibly loving.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:06.286
She's a nurse, so already, in my
mind, those are the best people.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.621
-Yes. And they have to be very
patient and forgiving, yeah.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.623
[ Applause ]
Yeah, give it up for nurses.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.059
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:16.228
But then, on top of it,
she's got Pete as a son.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:18.898
-Yeah. So you're a little
forgiving there, yeah.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.337
-So I needed to understand,
what's that mind-set?

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.173
How do you get there?
I didn't really catch it.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.508
I played a much better person
than myself.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.110
-There you go.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.613
Also, this rarely happens,
but it happened tonight.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.450
You and Matthew McConaughey were
in a film together 10 years ago.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.620
-I know. I wanted to come out
and surprise him.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.988
-But it must be nice to see
someone, because obviously

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:45.624
you do films and you sort of --
your lives cross for

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:47.226
a very short period of time
and then you move on.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.628
It must have been nice to see
each other again.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.896
-Yeah, it was wonderful to see
him. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:54.266
We had a great time
on that movie.

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.568
But I didn't realize he's not
running for governor anymore.

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:57.670
-He's not running for governor,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.971
so it's open
if you want to do it.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.174
-Yeah.
-You can jump in right now.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.277
-This is just the serendipitous
moment I needed to announce it.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.980
Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.781
-I want to talk because
I didn't realize

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.084
he gave you your first role.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.085
We've talked very lovingly about
Garry Marshall

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.321
on this show before,
who was a wonderful director,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.723
who passed away in 2016.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.491
I was lucky enough to get
to work with him.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:21.060
And I love talking to people who
worked with him because he was

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.463
the kind of person that I feel
like is so rare in Hollywood --

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.532
genuinely a loving,
giving person.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.567
-Yes, yes.
-What did you work with him on?

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.037
And how did you find your way
in front of him to begin with?

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.205
-I worked with him
on "Flamingo Kid."

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:34.640
-Alright. A classic.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.241
-Yes! I think so.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:38.210
-And Matt Dillon stars in that.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.179
And it was a great job.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.514
That was -- I mean, I came
to it -- it was --

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:44.717
I was, like, fresh-off-the-boat
kind of thing.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.753
I was really, like --
I looked through Backstage

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:50.923
and I saw an ad
for go in and audition.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.359
And somehow I made it through
a bunch of rounds,

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:58.030
and then he chose me to have
just one line, which was great.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.099
Actually, I was promoted
to have one line.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.901
I was just chosen to be there.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.636
-Do you remember your one line?
-Yes.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.005
It was, "Oh, you're so drunk!"

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.206
-Great.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.707
-I mean, it's kind of
a great first line.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.710
-It's a great first line, yeah.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.511
-Yeah, but he I loved
working with.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.546
It was one of the best jobs,
really, I've ever had.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:15.581
It kind of spoiled me.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.616
It was at a beach club
all summer.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:20.720
Just got to wear a bikini
and hang out at the beach club

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.854
and be with the wonderful
Garry Marshall.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.189
-So you had one line,
but you were there

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.223
the whole summer?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.223
-Oh, that's the best kind
of gig.

00:05:25.223 --> 00:05:26.258
-Just floating around.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:27.627
Yeah, that's the best kind,
right?

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.661
-You must have thought in later
gigs like, "What's this?"

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:32.397
-A little. Yes.

00:05:32.397 --> 00:05:34.967
Too much heavy lifting.
-Yeah.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:38.204
What I liked about Garry is
he was lovingly honest.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.271
I don't know if you felt this.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:40.505
The first time I met with him

00:05:40.505 --> 00:05:41.841
was about this movie,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.309
and we were talking about it.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.344
And then it was just lovely,
and then he goes,

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.546
"There's not a part for you
in this movie."

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:48.947
And I was like, "What --"

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:51.183
He goes, "Maybe my next movie.
It was great meeting you."

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.819
And I was like, "I can't believe
I spent this whole time

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:55.888
talking with him about a movie
that he knew

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:56.922
the minute I walked in
there wasn't a part for me."

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.123
-That you weren't
the right person.

00:05:58.123 --> 00:05:59.625
-But then the next movie,
he did give me a call,

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.093
so that was very loving.
-A man of his word.

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:02.828
-A man of his word.
-Yes.

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:04.797
-Is it true, also --
You grew up in Brooklyn,

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.399
and we were talking about the
fact that you're in L.A. now.

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.133
But I meant to ask this

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.369
when we were talking about
"King of Staten Island."

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.671
You had never been to
Staten Island

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.038
despite being a New Yorker.

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.741
-I think I was there
at some point, yes.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.444
Probably was a little toddler,
and something, you know,

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.778
in the '70s,
I was there at some point.

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.747
-Gotcha.
-I hadn't been there in years.

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:24.716
-And in your return to it,
was it nice to have Pete

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:27.186
as sort of a tour guide
to the finer points of --

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.587
-He is the mayor.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.489
He is the mayor of
Staten Island.

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:31.757
That is for sure, yes.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.392
-Are people really happy
to see him?

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.661
-Oh, yeah. Yeah, people were
really happy to see him,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.896
and he knows
all the right pizza places

00:06:37.896 --> 00:06:39.365
and he knows where to eat.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:42.334
And, yeah, it's his home turf.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:43.836
I loved being there with him.
-That's great.

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:46.639
What about holiday plans?
What are you gonna do?

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.474
-I'm gonna eat a lot.
-Okay, great.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:49.541
And you get to come back here
for it.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:51.677
-Gonna loaf around a lot.
-Okay.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.546
Are your East Coast family
so happy when you come back?

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:56.282
-Yes, and I'm so happy
to see them.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:59.719
My brother's in L.A.
I'm in L.A. as of now.

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.287
But everyone else is here, so --
-That's great.

00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:04.423
-And we didn't have Christmas
last year.

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:06.959
-No. Last year was a huge dud,
so I'm really hoping --

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.728
This has got to be good enough
for two Christmases.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.930
-Yes. And we almost have
two Christmases,

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.332
'cause we have Christmas Eve we
celebrate with the Seven Fishes,

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.700
and then we still have
the next day.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.335
-So you do the whole thing.
-So we do the whole thing.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:18.737
-Alright! The Seven Fishes.
How about that?

00:07:18.737 --> 00:07:21.040
That's authentic right there.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.942
-Not easy to pull off anymore.

00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:25.211
-Thank you so much for being
here. Congrats on the movie.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.846
-Thank you for having me.
Happy holidays.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:29.414
-Happy holidays to you.
You guys, that's Marisa Tomei.

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:32.385
"Spider-Man: No Way Home" is in
theaters and IMAX this Friday.

